---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Privacy Policy Page
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — December"
  description="Privacy Policy for December CLI and Cloud."
  canonicalUrl="https://trydecember.com/privacy"
  activePath="/privacy"
  hideHeader={false}
  hideFooter={false}
>
  <!-- Main Container: Identical horizontal gap/margins to landing page and docs page -->
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[940px] px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-24 min-w-0">
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="flex items-center flex-wrap font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#090a0f] transition-colors">home</a>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">legal</span>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#090a0f] font-medium">[privacy]</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Article Layout: Spans full width matching landing page & docs structure -->
    <article class="w-full min-w-0">
      <!-- Document Header -->
      <header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl min-w-0">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-2">Effective: September 2026</div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-[#090a0f] leading-snug">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#52525b] leading-relaxed">
          Phasehumans Inc. (&ldquo;Phasehumans&rdquo;, &ldquo;December&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is committed to transparency
          and developer privacy. This policy details how we collect, handle, and protect your data
          across the December CLI and cloud platforms.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Markdown / Body Content -->
      <div class="docs-prose min-w-0 max-w-full text-[#52525b] text-sm sm:text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2>Architecture & Data Minimization</h2>
          <p>
            December operates in two modes. In <strong>local mode</strong>, the CLI executes tools directly on
            your machine — your file paths, environment variables, and repository commits remain exclusively
            on your device. When you initiate a <strong>cloud handoff</strong> (via <code>/handoff</code>),
            only the specific files necessary for the task are transferred via encrypted TLS 1.3 to an
            ephemeral micro-VM.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>We strictly limit data collection to what is required to authenticate users and fulfill agent runs:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account Identifiers:</strong> Email, name, and OAuth identifiers from authentication providers (GitHub, Google).</li>
            <li><strong>BYOK API Keys:</strong> API keys you store for routing queries to model providers. Keys are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM.</li>
            <li><strong>Session History:</strong> Conversation prompts, tool call logs, and diff summaries generated during cloud sessions.</li>
            <li><strong>Diagnostic Telemetry:</strong> Optional anonymous CLI performance metrics. Telemetry never captures file contents, usernames, or repository secrets, and can be disabled at any time.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Google OAuth & Limited Use Compliance</h2>
          <p>
            December's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">
              Google API Services User Data Policy
            </a>, including the <strong>Limited Use</strong> requirements.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you sign in to December using Google OAuth, we access your profile information (full name, email address, profile photo URL, and unique Google ID) solely to authenticate your identity, create and maintain your account, and communicate essential notifications. We do not sell Google user data, share Google user data with data brokers, or use Google user data for advertising.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>No Model Training</h2>
          <p>
            We do not use your private code, prompts, project repositories, or Google user data to train or fine-tune artificial intelligence or machine learning models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>BYOK Key Security</h2>
          <p>
            Your personal AI model credentials belong solely to your account. They are never combined across users,
            never logged in plaintext, and never visible to Phasehumans employees. Keys are encrypted with envelope
            encryption using hardware KMS before persisting in our database.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Cloud Sandboxes & Handoff</h2>
          <p>
            Remote sessions via <code>/handoff</code> run inside isolated micro-VMs with dedicated kernel isolation.
            No cross-session memory sharing or cross-tenant networking occurs. Sandboxes are destroyed and their
            volumes zeroed out upon completion or timeout.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-Party AI Providers</h2>
          <p>
            December sends prompts and relevant code context to the model provider you select (e.g., Anthropic,
            OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek, or OpenRouter). Under commercial terms with these providers, zero-data-retention
            and no-training policies are maintained for API requests. When using BYOK, your organization's direct
            agreements with the provider apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data Retention & Deletion</h2>
          <p>You maintain full authority to delete your data at any time:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Purge individual sessions or clear complete cloud histories from the web dashboard.</li>
            <li>Deleting your account immediately purges all credentials, BYOK tokens, session archives, and billing records.</li>
            <li>Inactive cloud snapshots and log entries are automatically deleted on a rolling 30-day lifecycle.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Security</h2>
          <p>
            All traffic between the CLI, web app, and cloud sandboxes is encrypted using TLS 1.3 with strict HSTS headers.
            Production infrastructure requires hardware MFA and multi-party authorization. Security reports can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:security@trydecember.com">security@trydecember.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your Rights & Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on your location, you may have rights under GDPR, CCPA, or other privacy laws, including
            the right to access, correct, port, or erase your personal information. To exercise any of these
            rights or ask privacy-related questions, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com">team@trydecember.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Navigation & Contact -->
      <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">
          Questions? <a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">team@trydecember.com</a>
        </span>
        <a
          href="/terms"
          class="group inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 p-2.5 border border-[#e2e8f0] bg-white hover:border-[#87b2f4] text-[#090a0f] transition-all"
        >
          <span>Terms of Service</span>
          <span class="text-[#94a3b8] group-hover:text-[#87b2f4] transition-colors">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
